* Passive and discrete component models for OPA1641 mic simulation
* ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

* 1N4148 small signal diode
* Parameters from ON Semiconductor / Vishay published SPICE data
.model 1N4148 D (Is=2.52n N=1.752 Rs=0.568 Ikf=0 Xti=3 Eg=1.11
+ Cj0=4p M=0.4 Vj=0.75 Fc=0.5 Isr=1.48n Nr=2 Bv=100 Ibv=100u Tt=11.54n)

* BZX55C56 — 56V zener diode
* Vz=56V at Iz=5mA, Zz~70Ω
.model BZX55C56 D (Is=1n N=1 Rs=10 Cj0=50p Bv=56 Ibv=5m Vj=0.6 M=0.4)

* NTE10/3 transformer model (used reversed: 3-turn section as primary)
* Model values come from the data sheet and from measurements of the part on
*   its own, not from fitting a measurement of the whole microphone (#132).
* Turns 1:3:10 (data sheet). DC resistance measured on the part with a meter:
*   red-blue (3-turn) 521Ω on one unit, 540Ω on another (red-black 1720Ω,
*   blue-black 1182Ω); white-yellow (1-turn) 42Ω.
* Primary inductance (red-blue, 3-turn section): 7.4H, derived from the data
*   sheet, which gives no inductance but a response of at most -2 dB from 20 Hz
*   to 20 kHz in the intended use (200Ω source on the 1-turn side, 10kΩ load on
*   the 10-turn side). Taking that -2 dB at 20 Hz and from the inductance alone:
*   source 200 + 42Ω, load (10k + 1720)/100Ω, so 79Ω across the 1-turn side,
*   which needs 103Ω of reactance at 20 Hz: 0.82 H on the 1-turn side, 7.4 H on
*   the 3-turn section (x 3^2). An assumption, until the transformer is measured
*   on its own.
* Core loss Rc = 3k across the 3-turn section: PROVISIONAL (#137). Neither the
*   data sheet nor published data gives a figure, and the model needs one: without
*   it C_DC and Lp resonate near 26 Hz undamped (+1.2 dB at 30 Hz), which the
*   measurement does not show. The value is inferred from whole-microphone
*   measurements, which the model otherwise does not take values from: the
*   3-turn wiring measured 8.8 dB above the full winding against 10.0 dB without
*   core loss (about 2.5 to 3k matches), and damping the bump takes about 4k.
*   Rc is taken as independent of frequency and level, which real core loss is
*   not. To be replaced by a measurement of the transformer on its own.
* Secondary inductance (white-yellow, 1-turn): 7.4 / 9 = 822mH  (Ls = Lp/n^2, n=3)
* Coupling k=0.99932: keeps the leakage inductance at (1 - k^2) x Lp = 10mH, where
*   it was with Lp = 0.5H and k = 0.99, so the change of Lp leaves the top end alone.
.subckt NTE10_3 PRI_A PRI_B SEC_P SEC_N
Rp1  PRI_A    PRI_A2   521
Lp   PRI_A2   PRI_B    7.4
Rc   PRI_A2   PRI_B    3k     ; PROVISIONAL core loss (#137)
Ls   SEC_P2   SEC_N    822m
Rs1  SEC_P    SEC_P2   42
K1   Lp Ls    0.99932
.ends NTE10_3

* L78L24 simplified model: ideal 24V regulator with dropout
* Input on IN, output on OUT, ground on GND
* Quiescent current: ~3mA (modeled as current source from IN to GND)
.subckt L78L24 IN OUT GND_PIN
Vreg  OUT  GND_PIN  24
Rout  IN   INT_IN   0.1
Iq    INT_IN GND_PIN 3m
.ends L78L24

* BZX55C68 — 68V zener diode (DZ1 HV clamp, replaces BZX55C56)
.model BZX55C68 D (Is=1n N=1 Rs=10 Cj0=50p Bv=68 Ibv=5m Vj=0.6 M=0.4)

* BAT54S — Schottky diode (each junction modeled individually)
* V_F ~0.2V at low-µA loads; used in active Dickson pump
* Parameters from op-txm-v3 / Vishay datasheet
.model BAT54S D (IS=1e-6 N=1.05 BV=100 RS=3)
